[38;2;124;124;124mfunctions in L¹. But {0,1}-valued functions are a closed subset of L¹. The [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mquestion is whether this subset is separable.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mL¹([0,1]) is separable (has countable dense subset, e.g., step functions with [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mrational endpoints and rational values, or polynomials with rational [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcoefficients). But a subset of a separable metric space need not be separable...[0m[38;2;124;124;124mwait, actually every subset of a separable metric space IS separable. That's a [0m
