[38;2;124;124;124mregularity): for any measurable A and ε > 0, there's an open set U ⊇ A with m(U [0m[38;2;124;124;124m\ A) < ε/2, and U is a countable union of open intervals; take a finite subunion[0m[38;2;124;124;124mcovering all but ε/2.[0m

